# Direct dependencies of `library ledger-client` (tools/ledger_client_dependencies_check.sh).
# One per line: <package>[:<component>]: <why the ledger client core needs it>.
# Every direct dependency must be listed here with a reason, so a new
# dependency is a reviewed edit. A Singular component, directory, filepath,
# unix, process, network, http-client, http-client-tls, wai, warp and
# cardano-tx-tools are refused even when listed.
aeson: JSON encodings of network time and trace events
base: the language
base16-bytestring: hex rendering of hashes in network time and traces
bytestring: raw bytes of facts, hashes and snapshots
cardano-ledger-alonzo: script purposes and execution-unit evaluation
cardano-ledger-api: transaction body and output lenses
cardano-ledger-conway: the Conway era
cardano-ledger-core: protocol parameters, UTxO and the transaction lens
cardano-slotting: slot, epoch and system-start types
containers: maps and sets of resolved inputs and trace events
contra-tracer: the tracer typed read events are emitted to
crypton: SHA-256 of the pinned network material
memory: byte-array conversion of digests
microlens: lenses over ledger transactions
ouroboros-consensus: era history for slot-to-time conversion
serialise: CBOR decoding of the era history
text: textual identities and trace fields
time: clocks and durations
transformers: the pure Except used to validate network time
